-- title:
--   Ends carried into W force τ-stability of W
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of `levelH q M'` — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field and with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$ (`hζA`); $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function over $\mathbb{Q}$) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and $j_C :=$ `jChartFin A K j` $= j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j_C)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Throughout, a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g \neq 0$ as a Laurent series, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*\!\big(\tau x\big)\cdot \big(g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big)^\wedge = \big(f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}\big)^\wedge$ on $q$-expansions, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q \\ q\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A K j` along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}} : \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld-chart rigidity input, whose conclusion has seven conjuncts) requires: for every point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$, and $y'$ supersingular in the same sense as $y$ above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\big)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germ}_Y : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the germ map through the chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, $c \in W$ and $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $\tau$ through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ each omitting one of the images of $X_0,X_1$, each containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing $a_i X_0 + b_i X_1$ plus an element of $(X_0,X_1)^2$, with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the images of $X_0,X_1$, containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing $X_0$ plus an element of $(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a \in C$, the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the image of the $j$-expansion under `qExpand L q`) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with this element minus $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ with at least one of $a,b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(\text{that element} - a_0))) = \mathrm{mk}_S(h)$.
--
--   Next, a specific point is fixed: $z \in X$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$ (`hy'`), supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`), and $y' = y$ as ideals (`hy'y`). Data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ of exactly the shape produced by `hArig` are fixed (with $u_1,v_1$ units, $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism of the completed stalk with $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$), and `hW₁` asserts for these data the seven conjuncts (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   An ideal $J \subseteq C$ is fixed which, by `hJ`, is the infimum over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ of the contraction along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the images of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$. Let $W \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C \le B$ and $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for any $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,k - 1)$ with kernel $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) that stabilises $W$, through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image of $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ under some such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that $b \in B$ is divisible by $\varpi$ as soon as all such translates of $b$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and that $W$ is $\tau$-stable whenever $\tau$ preserves $y$.
--
--   Finally, a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$ is fixed, characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to `ends` if and only if there is a non-zero $a \in J$ such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by all $x$ with $xa \in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, with every element of $y$ lying in $O$ a non-unit of $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$. The hypothesis `hperm` requires that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ stabilising $W$, every $O \in$ `ends` satisfies $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$ for some $O' \in$ `ends`.
--
--   The conclusion is a single statement: for every $O \in$ `ends`, every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ maps $O$ into $W$, then $W$ is $\tau$-stable, that is, $f \in W \iff \tau f \in W$ for all $f \in K$.
--
--   This is a step in the local analysis of the supersingular fibre of the full-level modular curve: the exceptional valuation ring $W$ attached to the blown-up supersingular chart is shown to be stabilised by any level automorphism that pushes one of the finitely many ends of the chart inside it, the level structure being the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-type group $H_1$ for a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$. It feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_and_stabilizer_and_valuativeCover_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_commonChart_and_stabilizer_and_valuativeCover_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), and uses the finiteness of the group of level automorphisms of $K$ arising from $\Gamma_0(M')$.
-- source:
